{"name":"Platinum Blonde","hex":"#f0e8d7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"platinum blonde","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative spelling of platinum blond A color of hair"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative spelling of platinum blond A woman with platinum blonde hair."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/platinum_blonde"}],"entries":[{"title":"Platinum Blonde (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum Blonde, known briefly as The Blondes, is a Canadian rock band that formed in Toronto, Ontario, in 1979. Vocalist Mark Holmes has been the only consistent member of the band since its inception."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/3_piece_with_1984.jpg/330px-3_piece_with_1984.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum_Blonde_(band)","wikidata":"Q3391985"},{"title":"Platinum Blonde (EP)","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum Blonde is the self-titled debut EP by Platinum Blonde released in 1983. The EP was only released on vinyl and cassette and is also known as Six Track Attack. It reached a high of #65 on the Canadian RPM charts in early 1984, before being subsequently re-released with four additional tracks as the full-length Standing in the Dark album in 1984."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/fc/Platinum_Blonde_%28EP%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum_Blonde_(EP)","wikidata":"Q7202337"},{"title":"Platinum","blocks":[{"text":"Platinum is a chemical element; it has symbol Pt and atomic number 78. It is a dense, malleable, ductile, highly unreactive, precious, silverish-white transition metal. Its name originates from Spanish platina, a diminutive of plata \"silver\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Platinum_crystals.jpg/330px-Platinum_crystals.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Platinum","wikidata":"Q880"},{"title":"Blond","blocks":[{"text":"Blond or blonde, also referred to as fair hair, is a human hair color characterized by low levels of eumelanin, the dark pigment. The resultant visible hue depends on various factors, but always has some yellowish color. The color can be from the very pale blond to reddish \"strawberry\" blond or golden-brownish (\"sandy\") blond colors. Occasionally, the state of being blond, and specifically the occurrence of blond traits in a predominantly dark or colored population are referred to as blondism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/330px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blond","wikidata":"Q202466"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Rock_Of_Fame_2.jpg/500px-Rock_Of_Fame_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e7/Rock_Of_Fame_2.jpg/500px-Rock_Of_Fame_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Canada's Walk Of Fame inductees Platinum Blonde Mark Holmes, Sergio Galli and Chris Steffler, Massey Hall Toronto, 2023.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARock_Of_Fame_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg/500px-Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg/500px-Platin_l%C3%B6st_sich_in_hei%C3%9Fem_K%C3%B6nigswasser.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_co